"The Blue Path - Italia.it (https://www.italia.it/en/liguria/la-spezia/sentiero-azzurro)\nciteturn42view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 days ago; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.italia.it/en/liguria/la-spezia/sentiero-azzurro\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 91\nL0: [Input: Search]\nL1: # The Blue Path\nL2: \nL3: [Input] [Input]\nL4: \nL5: cite0†Image: sentiero azzurro†tourismmedia.italia.it L6: \nL7: The best way to explore the Cinque Terre\nL8: \nL9: cite1†Riomaggiore , cite2†Manarola , cite3†Corniglia , cite4†Vernazza , cite5†Monterosso al Mare . It is impossible not to be left speechless by the disarming beauty of the Ligurian villages better known as the cite6†Cinque Terre : small hilltop towns overlooking the sea in the province of cite7†La Spezia that enchant tourists with their breathtaking views and colourful houses.\nL10: The best way to explore this slice of Liguria is by walking along the Blue Path. This gentle, approximately 12-kilometre trail is suitable for everyone, and it is so beautiful that you will forget to feel tired!\nL11: The easiest part to tackle is the first kilometre from Riomaggiore to Manarola, which is, not by chance, called the Via dell’Amore (Path of Love). From there, you can decide if you want to continue to Corniglia and then on to Vernazza. Between stops, make sure to set aside time to explore the villages, tuck into some focaccia or a plate of trofie pasta with pesto, or even treat yourself to an aperitif by the sea: after so much walking, you definitely deserve it!\nL12: The Blue Trail is not currently open to the public, but it should be fully accessible again in 2024. You have to pay for entry. You can reach the starting point in Riomaggiore by bus or train. If you are travelling by car, we recommend parking at the La Spezia train station and then taking public transport.\nL13: \nL14: [Button: ]\nL15: \nL16: Some information is provided by:\nL17: \nL18: cite8†Image: Sponsor Credit L19: \nL20: The Blue Path\nL21: \nL22: 19016 Vernazza SP, Italia\nL23: \nL24: Call +390187817059 cite9†Website†www.parconazionale5terre.it L25: #### Map\nL26: \nL27: ### Listen and travel\nL28: \nL29: cite10†Podcast powered by Loquis†www.loquis.com L30: \nL31: cite11†Discover more L32: #### Related articles\nL33: cite12†Sport Trekking in Liguria: 6 routes not to be missed 4 minutes cite13†UNESCO Cinque Terre: enchanting villages overlooking the sea in Liguria 4 minutes cite14†Tours and experiences How to make pesto: 4 cooking classes in Liguria 4 minutes cite15†Food and wine From Levante to Ponente, Ligurian cuisine in 11 stops 5 minutes cite16†Sea The Italian Riviera di Levante 2 minutes cite17†Nature Landscapes of Liguria Powered by: 4 minutes cite18†Spirituality The Via Francigena and Liguria: in the heart of the Lunigiana area 2 minutes cite19†Sport Surfing school in Liguria: the 5 spots on the Riviera 2 minutes cite20†Food and wine Ligurian sheep's milk cheese: stories of pastures, flocks and mountains 2 minutes cite21†Shopping Genoa, luxury shopping between Via Roma and the Galleria Giuseppe Mazzini 4 minutes cite22†Leisure The Aquarium of Genoa, a tour of the world under the sea 2 minutes cite23†Sport Liguria: a walk through the centuries in Val Gargassa 2 minutes cite24†Leisure Liguria: the adventure park on the roof of Genoa 3 minutes cite25†Food and wine Liguria, Genoa: 10 gastronomic experiences in the Ancient Maritime Republic 3 minutes cite26†Shopping Textile workshops of Via di Scurreria 3 minutes cite27†Food and wine Liguria, flavors suspended between land and sea Powered by: 3 minutes cite28†Villages 3 lesser-known villages near the Cinque Terre in Eastern Liguria Powered by: 9 minutes cite29†Villages Camogli 3 minutes cite30†Cultural cities Discovering Genoa, a maritime city with a glorious history 5 minutes cite31†Luxury Everything there is to know about the Genoa Boa